CHAPTER.VERS:
Now I make known to you

          {+}
         brothers, the good news which I preached to you

          {+}
        , which also you

          {+}
         received, in which also you

          {+}
         stand,

by which also you

          {+}
         are saved. For what reason did I preach the good news to you

          {+}
        ? Unless you

          {+}
         hold fast [to it], you

          {+}
         believed for nothing.

For I delivered to you

          {+}
         first of all that which also I received: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures;

Whether then [it is] I or they, so we preach, and so you

          {+}
         believed.

Now if Christ is preached that he has been raised from the dead, how do some say among you

          {+}
         that there is no resurrection of the dead?

and if Christ has not been raised, then our preaching is also vain, [and] your

          {+}
         faith is also vain.

and if Christ has not been raised, your

          {+}
         faith [is] useless; you

          {+}
         are yet in your

          {+}
         sins.

I protest by that glorifying in you

          {+}
        , brothers, which I have in Christ Jesus our Lord, I die daily.

Awake to soberness righteously, and don't sin; for some have no knowledge of God: I speak [this] to move you

          {+}
         to shame.

Look, I tell you

          {+}
         a mystery: We all will not sleep, but we will all be changed,

Therefore, my beloved brothers, be

          {+}
         steadfast, unmoveable, always abounding in the work of the Lord, since you

          {+}
         know that your

          {+}
         labor is not vain in the Lord.
